            {"section": "dpsp-intro", "title": "Introduction to DPSP (Part IV, Articles 36-51)",
             "text": "The Directive Principles of State Policy are guidelines for the State to follow while making laws and policies. They are not enforceable by any court but are fundamental to the governance of the country. They aim to establish a social and economic democracy. The State shall strive to promote the welfare of the people by securing and protecting as effectively as it may a social order in which justice, social, economic and political, informs all institutions of national life."},
